menu "vstreamer"

config VSTREAMER_RS_PIE
    bool "Reed-Solomon FEC encode with the PIE SIMD kernel"
    depends on SOC_CPU_HAS_PIE
    default n
    help
        Encode FEC parity with the ESP32-P4 PIE kernel instead of the table path: about 2.8x
        faster (k=21, 10 parity rows, 1403-byte shards: 2.7 ms vs 7.7 ms), which frees core
        time at strong FEC. Off by default: with it on, the hardware H.264 encoder slowed from
        about 28 to 25.5 fps at FEC 21/31 (encode_ms spikes to 41-47 ms) for a reason not yet
        understood. Turn it on where FEC encode, not the encoder, is the bottleneck.

endmenu
